{"dur":600,"ev":[{"t":1.6,"type":"voice","id":"p01","dlg":true,"sub":"Five bills. All hundreds.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":6.2,"type":"voice","id":"p02","dlg":true,"sub":"Same five serial numbers. Forty-six of each.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":12,"type":"voice","id":"y01","dlg":true,"sub":"I can explain.","who":"You"},{"t":15.4,"type":"voice","id":"p03","dlg":true,"sub":"Great. Start with the printer.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":20.2,"type":"voice","id":"y02","dlg":true,"sub":"There’s no printer. There’s a wallet.","who":"You"},{"t":24.9,"type":"voice","id":"n01","dlg":false,"sub":"To be fair, it was a very good wallet."},{"t":37.4,"type":"voice","id":"n02","dlg":false,"sub":"This is you. Thirty-one, rent due on Friday, and three dollars short of everything."},{"t":51,"type":"voice","id":"n03","dlg":false,"sub":"This is your wallet, the next morning."},{"t":55,"type":"voice","id":"y03","dlg":true,"sub":"Wait. What?","who":"You"},{"t":58.2,"type":"voice","id":"n04","dlg":false,"sub":"Five hundred dollars. In hundreds. You have never even held a hundred."},{"t":63.8,"type":"voice","id":"y04","dlg":true,"sub":"Okay. Okay. Nobody panic.","who":"You"},{"t":68.6,"type":"voice","id":"n05","dlg":false,"sub":"So you test it, like a scientist. A nervous scientist."},{"t":76.6,"type":"voice","id":"n06","dlg":false,"sub":"Sock drawer. Full."},{"t":88.6,"type":"voice","id":"n07","dlg":false,"sub":"Freezer. Full, and cold."},{"t":100.8,"type":"voice","id":"n08","dlg":false,"sub":"Taped shut. Full, and sticky."},{"t":104.6,"type":"voice","id":"n09","dlg":false,"sub":"Five hundred a day is three thousand five hundred a week."},{"t":109,"type":"voice","id":"n10","dlg":false,"sub":"A hundred and eighty-two thousand, five hundred a year. Tax-free, as far as you know."},{"t":123,"type":"voice","id":"b01","dlg":true,"sub":"Got anything smaller?","who":"Barista"},{"t":127,"type":"voice","id":"y05","dlg":true,"sub":"No. And I never will.","who":"You"},{"t":131,"type":"voice","id":"n11","dlg":false,"sub":"That one, at least, was true."},{"t":149,"type":"voice","id":"n12","dlg":false,"sub":"Day two, the good headphones. Day three, the good chair."},{"t":153.4,"type":"voice","id":"n13","dlg":false,"sub":"Day five, a kayak. You live on the fourth floor."},{"t":158,"type":"voice","id":"n14","dlg":false,"sub":"And every morning, five hundred more."},{"t":188.5,"type":"voice","id":"y06","dlg":true,"sub":"This coffee used to taste like a holiday.","who":"You"},{"t":193.6,"type":"voice","id":"b02","dlg":true,"sub":"It’s the same coffee.","who":"Barista"},{"t":197.6,"type":"voice","id":"y07","dlg":true,"sub":"I know. That’s the problem.","who":"You"},{"t":205,"type":"voice","id":"n15","dlg":false,"sub":"In 1978, psychologists asked lottery winners how happy they were."},{"t":210.8,"type":"voice","id":"n16","dlg":false,"sub":"They turned out no happier than people who hadn’t won."},{"t":214.6,"type":"voice","id":"n17","dlg":false,"sub":"It’s called hedonic adaptation. The amazing becomes normal. Fast."},{"t":222,"type":"voice","id":"n18","dlg":false,"sub":"By day forty, you have a new problem. You can’t spend it fast enough."},{"t":226.6,"type":"voice","id":"n19","dlg":false,"sub":"Hundreds pile up in shoe boxes. Then in the kayak."},{"t":236,"type":"voice","id":"y08","dlg":true,"sub":"I need a bank.","who":"You"},{"t":239.6,"type":"voice","id":"n20","dlg":false,"sub":"Oh, you do. And you really, really don’t."},{"t":266.5,"type":"voice","id":"t01","dlg":true,"sub":"Good morning. Depositing?","who":"Teller"},{"t":270.7,"type":"voice","id":"y09","dlg":true,"sub":"Twenty-three thousand dollars. In cash. Normal amount.","who":"You"},{"t":276.7,"type":"voice","id":"t02","dlg":true,"sub":"Over ten thousand in cash, I file a report with the government. It’s routine.","who":"Teller"},{"t":284.5,"type":"voice","id":"y10","dlg":true,"sub":"Then do nine thousand nine hundred today, and the rest tomorrow?","who":"You"},{"t":291.1,"type":"voice","id":"t03","dlg":true,"sub":"Splitting deposits to dodge the report is called structuring. That’s a crime.","who":"Teller"},{"t":298.8,"type":"voice","id":"y11","dlg":true,"sub":"Even if the money’s real?","who":"You"},{"t":302.8,"type":"voice","id":"t04","dlg":true,"sub":"Even if the money’s real.","who":"Teller"},{"t":306.9,"type":"voice","id":"n21","dlg":false,"sub":"True, by the way. And it wasn’t even your biggest problem."},{"t":311.2,"type":"voice","id":"n22","dlg":false,"sub":"Every banknote has its own serial number. One number, one note."},{"t":316.4,"type":"voice","id":"n23","dlg":false,"sub":"Yours had the same five numbers. Forty-six times each."},{"t":338,"type":"voice","id":"n24","dlg":false,"sub":"Fake money in America is a job for the Secret Service. It’s what they were founded for, in 1865."},{"t":346.4,"type":"voice","id":"p04","dlg":true,"sub":"Sir. Bring the bag.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":355,"type":"voice","id":"p05","dlg":true,"sub":"Where’s the printer?","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":359.2,"type":"voice","id":"y12","dlg":true,"sub":"It’s a wallet.","who":"You"},{"t":362.5,"type":"voice","id":"p06","dlg":true,"sub":"This is empty.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":366.2,"type":"voice","id":"y13","dlg":true,"sub":"It refills in the morning.","who":"You"},{"t":370.3,"type":"voice","id":"p07","dlg":true,"sub":"Of course it does.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":374.4,"type":"voice","id":"n25","dlg":false,"sub":"Here’s what Agent Pike was really worried about. Not you. Everyone."},{"t":380.4,"type":"voice","id":"n26","dlg":false,"sub":"If one wallet refills, you’re rich. If every wallet refills, nobody is."},{"t":386.4,"type":"voice","id":"n27","dlg":false,"sub":"Everyone has more money, but there’s the same amount of bread."},{"t":390.6,"type":"voice","id":"n28","dlg":false,"sub":"So bread goes up. Then up again."},{"t":399.6,"type":"voice","id":"n29","dlg":false,"sub":"In Germany in 1923, a loaf of bread cost 200 billion marks."},{"t":405.6,"type":"voice","id":"n30","dlg":false,"sub":"In Zimbabwe in 2008, prices doubled about once a day."},{"t":412.8,"type":"voice","id":"n31","dlg":false,"sub":"Money works because there isn’t much of it. Make it endless, and it’s just paper."},{"t":425,"type":"voice","id":"y14","dlg":true,"sub":"So I’m a threat to the economy?","who":"You"},{"t":429.4,"type":"voice","id":"p08","dlg":true,"sub":"You? America has over twenty trillion dollars. You’re a rounding error.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":437,"type":"voice","id":"y15","dlg":true,"sub":"Oh. That’s good.","who":"You"},{"t":440.4,"type":"voice","id":"p09","dlg":true,"sub":"You’re a threat to my paperwork.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":445.4,"type":"voice","id":"n32","dlg":false,"sub":"Also, found money counts as income. A court ruled on it in 1969, about a couple who found cash inside an old piano."},{"t":454.8,"type":"voice","id":"y16","dlg":true,"sub":"A piano?","who":"You"},{"t":457.9,"type":"voice","id":"p10","dlg":true,"sub":"The wallet stays here. Evidence.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":462.9,"type":"voice","id":"y17","dlg":true,"sub":"That’s fair.","who":"You"},{"t":469,"type":"voice","id":"n33","dlg":false,"sub":"Day eighty-one. No wallet. One kayak. One tax bill."},{"t":491,"type":"voice","id":"n34","dlg":false,"sub":"That night, the wallet slept in locker forty-six."},{"t":520.6,"type":"voice","id":"p11","dlg":true,"sub":"…Form.","who":"Agent Pike"},{"t":525,"type":"voice","id":"n35","dlg":false,"sub":"Agent Pike logged five hundred dollars every morning for the next three years. He never spent a cent of it."},{"t":532.6,"type":"voice","id":"n36","dlg":false,"sub":"People said he was the most honest man in the building. Also the most tired."},{"t":550,"type":"voice","id":"b03","dlg":true,"sub":"Got anything smaller?","who":"Barista"},{"t":554.2,"type":"voice","id":"y18","dlg":true,"sub":"Actually, yes.","who":"You"},{"t":562,"type":"voice","id":"n37","dlg":false,"sub":"The coffee tasted like a holiday again. It was never the coffee. It was the running out."},{"t":1.150000